$ jet check chain_later.jet
Error [jet.MoveWithoutMarker]: `add` takes `xs`, but `xs` is used again later
  --> chain_later.jet:18:20
    |
 18 |     out: start.add(xs).add(ys)
    |                    ^^
  --> chain_later.jet:19:11
    |
 19 |     print(xs.len() + ys.len())
    |           ^^ `xs` is used again here
 Why: `add` takes ownership of this argument, and a call never copies on its own, so `xs` has no value after this call
 Fix: Write `xs.copy()` to pass a copy and keep `xs`, or reorder so this call is the last use of `xs`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0209

